| # | Finding | Resolution |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Attempt identity scoped to no expander | Fixed. New §8.4.1 defines `:yin.ledger/attempt` as `[incarnation counter]`, carried in the addressed record (§8.2) and the event (§8.4). The incarnation is a new `:incarnation` field of the expander's `ctx`, minted by the composition at construction as the log medium's identity plus the log cursor at construction, never derived from a batch. The counter is a per-incarnation attempt counter advanced like `:alloc`, including for admission failures. A staged-flush retry reuses the identity because the record is part of the staged payload under the same `ctx`; a restart constructs a new expander, mints a new incarnation, and records replay as a distinct execution. The parent-record chain is unchanged and one record per attempt is preserved. |
| 2 | Harvest catalogue loses shared legacy definition identity | Fixed. §8.5's catalogue is now one entry per original definition, each entry the set of `[j path]` occurrences of that definition; harvested once, one ordinal `k` per group, every occurrence replaced by a stand-in with the same `:decl k`. Admission validation checks disjoint non-empty groups, exact coverage of every definition node, one symbol and one body address per group, and whole-group declaration. Tuple-native frontends emit singleton groups. §9.1's adapter derives groups from entity identity and must extend the `datoms->ast` recursion to carry path and entity id, which it does not today. §2.5's catalogue row and §10.4 were updated to match. |

Neither finding required an owner ruling. One cross-document dependency is stated in §10.3: the `:incarnation` field is an addition to `yin.vm.macro.md`'s `ctx` that this document cannot make there.

